<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Implementation Details and Model Configurations</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To provide full transparency on how Reverse Mutual Information (RMI) is calculated, we present the exact chat templates and system prompts used for both the strong and weak models.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">DeepSeek-Coder Template</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The following template follows the official convention for DeepSeek-Coder-Instruct.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="121.78" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 653.15 121.78" width="653.15"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,121.78) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#8080FF;" fill="#8080FF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 117.15 C 0 119.71 2.07 121.78 4.63 121.78 L 648.52 121.78 C 651.08 121.78 653.15 119.71 653.15 117.15 L 653.15 4.63 C 653.15 2.07 651.08 0 648.52 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2F2FF;" fill="#F2F2FF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 100.23 L 652.46 100.23 L 652.46 4.63 C 652.46 2.45 650.7 0.69 648.52 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 107.54)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:44.26em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="612.43"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:44.26em;">
<span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">System Template for DeepSeek-Coder</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 12.5)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:44.26em;--ltx-fo-height:5.49em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="75.91" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 75.91)" width="612.43"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:44.26em;">
<span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">System<span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">: You are an AI programming assistant, utilizing the Deepseek Coder model, developed by Deepseek Company, and you only answer questions related to computer science. For politically sensitive questions, security and privacy issues, and other non-computer science questions, you will refuse to answer. 
<br class="ltx_break"></span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Qwen3 Template</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For Qwen3-0.6B, we use a consistent system prompt to focus the model on computer science tasks. Note that for this model, we explicitly set <span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">enable_thinking=False</span> to maintain standard autoregressive behavior.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="107.87" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 653.15 107.87" width="653.15"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,107.87) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#8080FF;" fill="#8080FF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 103.24 C 0 105.8 2.07 107.87 4.63 107.87 L 648.52 107.87 C 651.08 107.87 653.15 105.8 653.15 103.24 L 653.15 4.63 C 653.15 2.07 651.08 0 648.52 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2F2FF;" fill="#F2F2FF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 86.31 L 652.46 86.31 L 652.46 4.63 C 652.46 2.45 650.7 0.69 648.52 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 93.63)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:44.26em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="612.43"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:44.26em;">
<span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">System Template for Qwen3</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 15.19)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:44.26em;--ltx-fo-height:4.29em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="62" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 59.31)" width="612.43"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:44.26em;">
<span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">System<span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">: You are an AI programming assistant, and you only answer questions related to computer science. For politically sensitive questions, security and privacy issues, and other non-computer science questions, you will refuse to answer.</span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Implementation Note</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In both cases, <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{PPL}(Q|A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>PPL</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{PPL}(Q|A)</annotation></semantics></math> is calculated by performing a forward pass on the ground-truth question tokens represented by <span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">[Q]</span> in the Assistant turn, while teacher-forcing the System and User inputs as context.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Sensitivity to Chat Template and Task Framing</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We investigate how specific task instructions and formatting affect RMI and IFD signals.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Standard Implementations (Template-based).</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In our main experiments, both metrics utilize structured chat templates. For **Standard RMI**, the reverse generation task is highly constrained: <span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">‘‘TASK: Given an answer, generate the most likely <span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">computer science</span> question that this answer is responding to. If the inferred question is outside computer science, respond with <span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">‘INVALID’</span>.’’</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For **Template-based IFD**, we compute the perplexity of the answer <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> within the following structured templates:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="118.67" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 653.15 118.67" width="653.15"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,118.67) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#8080FF;" fill="#8080FF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 114.05 C 0 116.6 2.07 118.67 4.63 118.67 L 648.52 118.67 C 651.08 118.67 653.15 116.6 653.15 114.05 L 653.15 4.63 C 653.15 2.07 651.08 0 648.52 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2F2FF;" fill="#F2F2FF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 114.05 C 0.69 116.22 2.45 117.98 4.63 117.98 L 648.52 117.98 C 650.7 117.98 652.46 116.22 652.46 114.05 L 652.46 4.63 C 652.46 2.45 650.7 0.69 648.52 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 13.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:44.26em;--ltx-fo-height:6.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.08em;font-size:10pt;" height="93.67" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 92.52)" width="612.43"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:44.26em;">
<span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">System<span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.pic1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">: Standard system prompt 
<br class="ltx_break"></span>User<span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.pic1.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">: [None] 
<br class="ltx_break"></span>Assistant<span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.pic1.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">: <span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.pic1.1.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">[A]</span></span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="118.67" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 653.15 118.67" width="653.15"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,118.67) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#8080FF;" fill="#8080FF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.63 L 0 114.05 C 0 116.6 2.07 118.67 4.63 118.67 L 648.52 118.67 C 651.08 118.67 653.15 116.6 653.15 114.05 L 653.15 4.63 C 653.15 2.07 651.08 0 648.52 0 L 4.63 0 C 2.07 0 0 2.07 0 4.63 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2F2FF;" fill="#F2F2FF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 4.63 L 0.69 114.05 C 0.69 116.22 2.45 117.98 4.63 117.98 L 648.52 117.98 C 650.7 117.98 652.46 116.22 652.46 114.05 L 652.46 4.63 C 652.46 2.45 650.7 0.69 648.52 0.69 L 4.63 0.69 C 2.45 0.69 0.69 2.45 0.69 4.63 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 20.38 13.66)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:44.26em;--ltx-fo-height:6.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.08em;font-size:10pt;" height="93.67" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 92.52)" width="612.43"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:44.26em;">
<span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">System<span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.pic1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">: Standard system prompt 
<br class="ltx_break"></span>User<span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.pic1.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">: <span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.pic1.1.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">[Q]</span> 
<br class="ltx_break"></span>Assistant<span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.pic1.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">: <span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.pic1.1.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">[A]</span></span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Variations for Sensitivity Analysis.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To isolate the impact of task framing, we compare our standard method against several variations:</p>
<ul id="A2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Raw IFD</span>: Following the original implementation proposed by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al. (2024b)</a></cite>, Raw IFD is computed via simple text concatenation: <span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">[Q] + [A]</span> for the conditional part, and <span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">[A]</span> for the unconditional part, without any system prompts or role indicators (User/Assistant).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Simplified Task Prompt (<math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=0.88" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.88</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=0.88</annotation></semantics></math>)</span>: Removes both the domain specificity and the negative constraint, using a more general instruction: <span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">‘‘TASK: Given an answer, generate the most likely question that this answer is responding to.’’</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">System Context Only (<math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=0.79" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.79</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=0.79</annotation></semantics></math>)</span>: For <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="PPL(Q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">PPL(Q)</annotation></semantics></math>, we retain the System Prompt but <span id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">remove the explicit “TASK” instruction</span>. This tests whether the model’s persona alone (e.g., “You are an AI assistant”) is sufficient for estimating query probability.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prefix-only (<math id="A2.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=0.70" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.70</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=0.70</annotation></semantics></math>)</span>: For <math id="A2.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="PPL(Q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">PPL(Q)</annotation></semantics></math>, we strip away the System Prompt and use only a minimal newline-delimited indicator (<span id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">"Question:"</span>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pure Raw (<math id="A2.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=0.62" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.62</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=0.62</annotation></semantics></math>)</span>: For <math id="A2.I1.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="PPL(Q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">PPL(Q)</annotation></semantics></math>, we calculate the perplexity from the very first token of the query with <span id="A2.I1.i5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">zero context</span> (cold start).</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Results and Analysis.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As shown in Table <a href="#A2.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ Results and Analysis. ‣ Appendix B Sensitivity to Chat Template and Task Framing ‣ QAQ: Bidirectional Semantic Coherence for Selecting High-Quality Synthetic Code Instructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, IFD is remarkably stable (<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=0.957" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.957</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=0.957</annotation></semantics></math>) even under raw concatenation. In contrast, RMI drops as we strip away the template and context. The correlation decreases from 0.88 (Simplified Template) to 0.79 (System-Prefix), 0.70 (Prefix-only), and 0.62 (Pure Raw). This confirms that while the specific <span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">wording</span> of the template matters less, the presence of <span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">sufficient context</span> for <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="PPL(Q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">PPL(Q)</annotation></semantics></math> is critical. Even without a task template, providing the system prompt (<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=0.79" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.79</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=0.79</annotation></semantics></math>) significantly stabilizes the metric compared to raw inputs.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T4" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A2.T4.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A2.T4.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T4.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="A2.T4.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Comparison (vs. Standard RMI)</span></th>
<th id="A2.T4.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="A2.T4.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Spearman <math id="A2.T4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math></span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A2.T4.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T4.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">IFD vs. Raw IFD</td>
<td id="A2.T4.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">0.957</td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T4.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T4.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">RMI vs. Simplified Task Prompt</td>
<td id="A2.T4.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.88</td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T4.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T4.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">RMI vs. System-Prefix (No Template)</td>
<td id="A2.T4.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.79</td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T4.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T4.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">RMI vs. Prefix-only (No Template)</td>
<td id="A2.T4.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.70</td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T4.2.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T4.2.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">RMI vs. Pure Raw (No Template)</td>
<td id="A2.T4.2.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">0.62</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4: </span>Spearman correlation of metrics under different task framings.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The primary source of instability is the <span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">contextual imbalance in <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="PPL(Q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">PPL(Q)</annotation></semantics></math> calculation</span>. In the <span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Pure Raw</span> setting, the model must predict the query from a "cold start" without knowing it is handling a CS query. Since queries are typically short, the high loss incurred by the initial tokens dominates the average <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="PPL(Q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">PPL(Q)</annotation></semantics></math>, biasing the <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="RMI" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">RMI</annotation></semantics></math> upwards and introducing noise (see Figure <a href="#A2.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ Discussion: Why IFD is More Robust. ‣ Appendix B Sensitivity to Chat Template and Task Framing ‣ QAQ: Bidirectional Semantic Coherence for Selecting High-Quality Synthetic Code Instructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Discussion: Why IFD is More Robust.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">IFD remains robust because <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="PPL(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">PPL(A)</annotation></semantics></math> is calculated on answer sequences (code) that are typically longer and follow familiar structural patterns (<span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">def</span>, <span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">import</span>). Moreover, <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is always conditioned on <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> in the IFD calculation, avoiding the "zero context" problem. The correlation jump from 0.62 to 0.70 by simply adding a <span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">"Question:"</span> indicator proves that task framing is essential for RMI to capture genuine semantic coherence rather than prefix-induced surprise.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F5" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2603.12165v1/fig_rmi_vs_raw_rmi.png" id="A2.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:381/354;" width="381" height="354" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 5: </span>Scatter plot comparing Standard RMI vs. Raw RMI. The lack of system context in the Raw version leads to inflated <math id="A2.F5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="PPL(Q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">PPL(Q)</annotation></semantics></math> and subsequent overestimation of RMI.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
</article>
</div>
</div>
